// Secrets configuration for AnyRank.
//
// Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` (which is gitignored) and fill in your
// own values. The Xcode build picks the file up via Project.yml's
// `baseConfiguration` setting, then injects the values into Info.plist at
// build time. Empty values are allowed during development — sign-in will
// fail with a "missing client ID" error, which is the expected behavior
// when running locally without OAuth wired up.
//
// To get the Google OAuth client ID:
//   1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
//   2. Create (or pick) a project. Configure the OAuth consent screen.
//   3. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID. Application type: iOS.
//      Bundle ID: com.ellismiranda.anyrank.AnyRank (or whatever you set in Project.yml).
//   4. Copy the Client ID into GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID below.
//   5. Take that same client ID, split on `.`, reverse the parts, and join
//      with `.` — that's GOOGLE_OAUTH_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID. The Google console
//      also shows this value directly as "iOS URL scheme."
//
// Examples (these are fake — do not use):
//   GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID = 1234567890-abc123def456.apps.googleusercontent.com
//   GOOGLE_OAUTH_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID = com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abc123def456

GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID =
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID =

// Google Places API key. Required for Restaurants/Bars/Custom-with-Maps
// search. The Places SDK is API-key gated (not OAuth-gated); the sign-in
// requirement surfaced to users in the search screen is a UX gate that
// lives on top.
//
// To get the key:
//   1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials in the same
//      project you used for the OAuth client ID above.
//   2. Enable the "Places API" (and "Places API (New)" if you want the
//      newer endpoints) under APIs & Services > Library.
//   3. Create an API key under Credentials. Restrict it: iOS app
//      restriction with bundle ID com.ellismiranda.anyrank.AnyRank, and API
//      restriction limited to the Places API.
//   4. Paste it below.
//
// Leaving this empty falls back to MockPlacesSearchService at runtime —
// the search screens stay functional with the canned dataset.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY =

// TMDB read access token. Required for live movie search. Movies auto-fall
// back to MockMovieSearchService when this is empty.
//
// To get the token:
//   1. Create a free account at https://www.themoviedb.org
//   2. Under Settings > API, request an API key. Fill in an application URL
//      (a GitHub repo or personal site is fine) and a short description.
//   3. Approval is essentially instant for non-commercial use.
//   4. Copy the "API Read Access Token" (the long JWT-style string) below —
//      NOT the shorter v3 API key. The Live service uses Bearer auth.
TMDB_READ_TOKEN =

// Twitch client credentials — required for live video-game search
// via IGDB. Twitch owns IGDB and gates it behind their OAuth 2.0
// client-credentials flow (app-level, no user login). Leaving both
// empty falls back to MockGameSearchService.
//
// To get them:
//   1. https://dev.twitch.tv/console → Register Your Application.
//     - OAuth Redirect URL: http://localhost (unused for client-credentials)
//     - Category: Application Integration
//   2. Copy the Client ID and generate a Client Secret.
//   3. Enable IGDB usage under the same app if prompted.
TWITCH_CLIENT_ID =
TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET =

// Spotify client credentials — required for live music search (both
// Albums and Songs). Search-only usage doesn't need per-user OAuth;
// client credentials (app-level) is enough. Missing values fall back
// to MockMusicSearchService.
//
// To get them:
//   1. https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard → Create app.
//     - Redirect URI: http://localhost (unused for client-credentials)
//     - API/SDKs used: Web API
//   2. Open the app's Settings → copy Client ID + Client Secret.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID =
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET =

// Steam Web API key — reads a user's owned games for the Steam import.
// Without it, the Steam import runs against a built-in sample library.
//
// To get one: https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey (any domain name works
// for a personal key). The user's Steam profile must have "Game details"
// set to Public for their library to be readable.
STEAM_WEB_API_KEY =

// Future entries — uncomment and fill when the corresponding live services
// are wired up. See https://github.com/elsmrna/anyrank/issues/1.
